					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Two years later but just on the record, would like to say I agree. A nice balance is what I think defines SCP Foundation, the lethal and the harmless, aggressive and the skips not meaning harm with what they do. In a world like that, it'd make sense that something less dangerous while also massively entertaining could exist. I mean, it's crazy weird stuff with play-doh. Won't make something super deadly but certainly fun for kids. Except y'know, choking hazard.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
