				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-142344#post-1539203</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-142344/scp-705#post-1539203</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 16 Aug 2012 14:47:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>daioni</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1287530</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>&quot;I go on a hiatus and what happens while I'm gone? Bright gets himself an army of Play-Doh Men! You lucky bastard.&quot;</p> <p>This is pretty much exactly why I'm downvoting this. It isn't written badly and the concept is alright, but these things generally aren't supposed to be &quot;cool&quot; or &quot;desirable&quot;, and they damn well aren't supposed to belong to one Doctor or another (at least in my view of things). A reference to interaction here or there is fine, but when you have the things declaring outright loyalty to someone that's crossing the line. Same issue I had with 237.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
